Z||000000||saleenfiero||03-20-2001||01:47 PM||||I have two racing stripes that were put on my car a while ago and now I want them OFF.<BR>Problem is they were made from 3M sign vinyl (same stuff they put on street signs).  Any idea on how to get this off?  <P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||13
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-20-2001||01:58 PM||||i get a lot of decals off by letting them soak with wd40. if that dont work use a hairdryer to heat them and pull them gently and steady. You will prob have some glue residue that will come off with alcohol. dont be surprized if under the stripe its now a different color after your paints faded.||||reg||1
Z||000002||webbee||03-20-2001||03:20 PM||||I use lighter fluid (naptha) in an oiler can. It doesn't screw up the paint. Yes the paint under the decal will be a different color.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mi Junk||03-20-2001||03:53 PM||||3M makes a disc for removing decals. They come in a kit of 3 w/ the adapter. They're kind of pricey, but work really well and they do not hurt the finish.<BR>Oh ya they make one hell of a mess - little white pieces everywhere, but like I said they work great ( I remove some big decal on a Fiero I had.)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000004||RRobinson||03-20-2001||05:38 PM||||I use a heat gun and my fingernails to get the decals off, then varsol or a similar product to get the glue residue off. I took off the huge, gross, grey, black and pink graphics package off my 87 SE this way. Looks good now. I could not believe someone would deface that car with those graphics! I was actually embarassed driving the thing home &lt;Shudder&gt;<P>Ryan <BR>88 GT Red<BR>87 GT Blue <BR>87 GT Black<BR>87 SE V6 Med. red||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||03-20-2001||05:50 PM||||First you boil water for about 20 minutes.  Oh wait, that's for those ricey decals.  Different recipe.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||03-21-2001||09:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mi Junk:<BR><B>3M makes a disc for removing decals. They come in a kit of 3 w/ the adapter.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have heard about those before, and I was wanting to try one to get the pinstriping off my coupe before I paint it...where did you get yours at?<P>3M also makes an emblem and trim adhesive remover, works very well, I have used it on many car paint projects.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||03-21-2001||10:26 AM||||there like a pencil eraser, u put them in a drill. I use the big one ,its about 3 inches in diameter. Still takes a little while. there really good for pinstripes but takes forever on a big decal. The WD40 you just spray and leave it for a few hours and usually they almost fall off.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mi Junk||03-21-2001||11:26 PM||||FieroJoe, I think I got them from automotive paint shop. Something like $30-$40 Cdn per kit.<BR>Right now I'm doing work for 3M Canada in London. They have a in plant store with some really good deals I've been looking for the kit myself just to have. If I come across some cheap I'll let you know.||||reg||6
